  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Technical Symposium - 2013 U.S. China Aviation Symposium, through American Association of Airport Executives</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">USTDA funding of $325,000 is supporting the U.S.- China Aviation Symposium, a two and half-day conference held in Beijing China in late 2013. This symposium builds upon themes from previous U.S.- China aviation events, with focus on key areas such as air traffic management and safety, emissions reduction, air traffic control capacity and efficiency, general aviation, air navigation and communications systems, air cargo infrastructure and green airport development. It targets up to 250 attendees, including senior government officials from the United States and China, as well as representatives from the U.S. aviation industry.</narrative>
  </description>
